  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SPAS-Building sustainable peace in Myanmar 2014-18 - Building sustainable peace in Myanmar</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Svenska Freds Byggande av varaktig fred i Myanmar 2014-18</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased participation and influence of women, youth and ethnic minorities in local and regional peace processes in Myanmar.
Feeding up to that main outcome are a number of bridging outcomes:
1. Women, youth and ethnic minorities from the target groups will have increased participation in local and regional peace processes.
2. One organisation in the project will have established a helpdesk office for conflict analyses, early warning and response systems, sharing best practices and lessons learned, conflict impact assessments, interfaith and diversity expertise.
3. Increased debate and acknowledgement in the Myanmar public domain and the international community, on women, youth and ethnic minorities&apos; rights to have political influence in local, regional and national peace processes.
4. Civil society actors within the programme will contribute to preventing local and regional conflicts between four local groups in Chin state / Sagaing region.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sida makes the assessment that the programme &quot;Building sustainable peace in Myanmar&quot; during the period 2014-2017, presented on behalf of the Swedish Peace- and Arbitration Society, SPAS, is highly relevant in relation to the Swedish Results Strategy for international developement cooperation in Myanmar 2013-2017. The overall objective of the programme is aligned to the results area of &quot;Broad popular partcipation in the peace process&quot; and the specific result to gain &quot;Increased participation of women and ethnic minorities in the peace process.&quot; 

The programme will be implemented by SPAS and the umbrella organisation AYO SDA in Myanmar in cooperation with eight local, community based organisations. The activities will consist of seminars, awareness-raising initiatives and advocacy work related to peace building and will be realised in 14 of the most conflict-affected areas in the country.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Svenska Freds- och Skiljedomsf&#xf6;reningen kommer att under perioden 2014-2017 att genomf&#xf6;ra programmet &quot;Byggande av varaktig fred i Myanmar&quot;. Den &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;ls&#xe4;ttningen med programmet &#xe4;r att bidra till kvinnors, ungas och etniska minoriteters &#xf6;kade delaktighet och p&#xe5;verkan i de lokala, regionala och nationella fredsprocesserna i landet. Programmet pr&#xe4;glas av en fredsbyggande ansats med ett lokalt, gr&#xe4;srotsperspektiv i grunden. Programmet har utformats och kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras i n&#xe4;ra samverkan med paraplyorganisationen Ar Yone Oo Social Development Association, AYO SDA, och &#xe5;tta organisationer med varierande profil inom fred- och konfliktfr&#xe5;gor, m&#xe4;nskliga r&#xe4;ttigheter, ickev&#xe5;ld, kvinnor och urfolks r&#xe4;ttigheter, r&#xe4;ttvist naturresursutnyttjande. Aktiviteter planeras i 14 av de mest konfliktdrabbade regionerna i Myanmar. Initiativet inneb&#xe4;r bland annat seminarier, kapacitetsutvecklande insatser samt p&#xe5;verkansarbete riktat mot politiker och policyfunktioner.</narrative>
  </description>
